Subject: report how much memory the engine is currently holding

What this does
  Adds a way to ask the engine how many bytes it has allocated right now.
  It reads a number the engine already keeps, so it costs nothing to call.

Why we need it
  The runtime decides when to collect garbage based on how much memory is
  live. There was already a way to measure memory, JS_ComputeMemoryUsage, but
  it walks the whole heap to produce its answer. That is far too expensive to
  call on every check, which is exactly where we need the number.

What it adds
  JS_GetMallocSize()  - the number of bytes the engine has allocated.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 55f7c76..b7d53e5 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -7453,6 +7453,11 @@ static void gc_free_cycles(JSRuntime *rt)
     init_list_head(&rt->gc_zero_ref_count_list);
 }
 
+size_t JS_GetMallocSize(JSRuntime *rt)
+{
+    return rt->malloc_state.malloc_size;
+}
